The best interval we can use (the interval whose points are given that's closest to $x=-9$) is the interval between $x=-10$ and $x=-8$. Let's find the average rate of change between those points.

$\begin{align}
h'(-9)&\approx\dfrac{h(-8)-h(-10)}{-8-(-10)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-88-(-85)}{2}
\\\\
&=-1.5
\end{align}$
